---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const description =
  'What mybankjobs is, how the data works, and how to reach us. An independent, free, ad-free index of official South African bank vacancies.';
---

<Base title="About — mybankjobs" description={description} narrow>
  <a class="backlink" href="/">← All vacancies</a>
  <div class="prose">
  <h1>About mybankjobs</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    One page that gathers every official South African bank vacancy, straight from the banks' own
    career systems — so you don't have to check each site one by one.
  </p>

  <h2>What this is</h2>
  <p>
    mybankjobs reads the banks' own career systems a few times a day and lists what's genuinely
    open, in one place. Every job links back to the bank's official application page. There are no
    recruiter reposts, no duplicates, and no expired ads — if a bank closes a job, it comes off this
    site.
  </p>
  <p>
    We never take your CV or personal details. The apply button always sends you to the bank's own
    official application page, where the actual application happens. This is a free service: no ads,
    no sponsored listings, no accounts, and nothing to sell.
  </p>

  <h2>Not affiliated with any bank</h2>
  <p>
    mybankjobs is an independent service and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or acting on
    behalf of any bank. Bank names are used only to identify whose public vacancies are listed. All
    applications happen on the banks' own official websites.
  </p>

  <h2>How the data works</h2>
  <p>
    A few times a day we fetch each covered bank's public vacancy feed and compare it to what we
    already have. New roles are added; roles that have disappeared from the bank's system are
    removed.
  </p>
  <p>
    To avoid flicker from a single hiccup, a job is only marked closed after it has been absent from
    the bank's system for two consecutive checks. As a backstop, anything we cannot re-confirm
    within 60 days is taken down regardless — we would rather show nothing than show a stale job. The
    “last updated” time at the top of every page is real; if a fetch ever breaks, that time will
    show it.
  </p>
  <p>
    South African roles are shown by default. Some banks also advertise roles outside South Africa;
    those are kept on a separate <a href="/browse/international">international roles</a> page and
    clearly marked, never mixed into the default lists.
  </p>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    No accounts, no cookies, no tracking. We don't ask for your details and we have nothing to log
    you into. At most we use privacy-friendly, cookieless analytics to count page views in
    aggregate — never anything that identifies you.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact and takedowns</h2>
  <p>
    Something wrong, or listing your organisation's jobs and want them removed? Email
    <a href="mailto:tebellonamo@gmail.com">tebellonamo@gmail.com</a> — requests are honoured promptly.
  </p>
  </div>
</Base>
